
For more information on a specific command, type "HexmodX.cmd -help CommandName"

                                          Basic Input - Output Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
READ           |    Reads hex file of type ".hex", ".s19" and ".bin".               |    
READATA        |    READATA command reads data from a hex file with a particular address and length.
WRITE          |    Writes output hex file of type ".hex", ".s19" and ".bin". 
WRITEADDRESS   |    Writes the data at the given address.              
WRITERANGE     |    Serialize a range of data.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                            Patch Check View Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH          |    Patches data of type IHEX, ASCII or reference data at a particular address.
CHECK          |    Checks for data of type IHEX, ASCII or reference data at a particular address.
VIEW           |    View data at a particular address.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                 Memory Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEMCOPY        |    Copies a range of data from source to destination address within same hex file.
MEMMOVE        |    Moves a range of data from source to destination address within same hex file.
MEMDELETE      |    Deletes a range of data.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                  Fill Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILLV          |    Fills gaps within specified range with user defined byte or default value "0x00".
FILLP          |    Fills specified range with user defined byte value or default value "0x00".
FILLALL        |    Fills all the gaps in the hex file or from a given start address till the end of that file.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                Infoblock Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BLKBUILD       |    Builds the already linked Infoblocks for processing.
BLKLINK        |    Links list of Infoblocks provided by the BLKLINK command.
DETAILEDLOG    |    Logs the basic infoblock structure into an xml file.
INFOTABLELOG   |    Logs the Infotable information of each Infoblock into an xml file.
DELETEBLOCK    |    Deletes an infoblock.
LOG            |    Logs information of the basis infoblock and checksum entries.
WRITECKS       |    Sets or tests Infoblock Checksum and ChecksumBlock Checksum.
SWID           |    Sets or test SWID field within each Infoblock.
SWTTNR         |    Sets or tests SWTTNR field within each Infoblock.
VALIDPATTERN   |    Sets or tests VALIDPATTERN field.
COMP           |    Sets or tests compatibility between infoblocks 
COMPRESET      |    Reset compatibility between infoblocks.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                ABM - BMI Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ABM            |    Performs ABM and BMI build
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                               Conversion Operations

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME   |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONVERT        |    Coverts supported hex file format into ".hex", ".s19" and ".bin" format.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                CONFIG-HEXMOD Operations

-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND NAME                   |    DESCRIPTION
-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_MERGE_CLEAN_CHECKSUM    |    MERGE CLEAN CHECKSUM FOR CONFIG HEXMOD.
CONFIG_SPLIT_REF               |    SPLIT REF FUNCTIONALITY FOR CONFIG HEXMOD.
CONFIG_CB_MERGE                |    MERGE FUNCTIONALITY FOR CB.
CONFIG_CLEAN                   |    CLEAN FUNCTIONALITY FOR CONFIG HEXMOD.
CONFIG_MERGE                   |    MERGE FUNCTIONALITY FOR CONFIG HEXMOD.
CONFIG_SPLIT                   |    SPLIT FUNCTIONALITY FOR CONFIG HEXMOD.
CONFIG_GENERAL                 |    GENERAL SWITCHES IN CONFIG HEXMOD.
-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    
                                                    CLEANUP COMMAND

------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION                                                      
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------
   -blockaddress  |    Start address of the block in the input hex file.                
   -filename      |    Output file name.                                                
   -type          |    Type of output HEX file. By default it is IHEX                   
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                    COMPRESS COMMAND

------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION                                                      
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -startaddress  |    Start address to be compressed.                                      
   -endaddress    |    End address to be compressed.                                        
   -at            |    Destination address where the compressed data will be placed.        
   -outputfile    |    Output file name of the compressed hex file.                         
   -type          |    Type of input HEX file.                                              
   -fillpattern   |    Pattern to be filled in the gaps.                                    
   -range         |    Specifies the number of data ranges to be compressed.                
   -lyt           |    Layout of the output hex file.                                       
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                    DECRYPT COMMAND

------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION                                                      
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------
   -startaddress  |    Start address to be  decrypted.                                  
   -endaddress    |    End address to be  decrypted.                                    
   -key           |    Key value.                                                       
   -vector        |    Vector value.                                                    
   -algo          |    Type of algorithm.                                               
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                    ENCRYPT COMMAND

------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION                                                      
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------
   -startaddress  |    Start address to be  encrypted.                                  
   -endaddress    |    End address to be  encrypted.                                    
   -key           |    Key value.                                                       
   -vector        |    Vector value.                                                    
   -algo          |    Type of algorithm.                                               
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                MDG1TPORT HASH COMMAND

----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES              |    DESCRIPTION                                                                  
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -input             |    Input hex file name.                                                         
   -output            |    Output Hash file name.                                                       
   -igcks             |    Ignores line checksum while parsing the input hex file.                      
   -filetype          |    Input hex file type.                                                         
   -id                |    ID given to the hash for of each range.                                      
   -division          |    Specifies the division type.                                                 
   -HSMfile           |    HSM file name.                                                               
   -HSMconfig         |    HSM configuration type.                                                      
   -tctype            |    Trust center type Eg. BOSCH TRUST CENTER, VW TRUST CENTER                    
   -mode              |    Mode type eg. Online or Offline.                                             
   -oidpub            |    OID value.                                                                   
   -infoblockaddress  |    Infoblock start address.                                                     
   -infoblockcount    |    Infoblock count for which hash value to be calculated.                       
   -rangecount        |    Total number of count for range where hash value to be calculated.           
   -startaddress      |    Start address of the range in hex file.                                      
   -endaddress        |    End address of the range in hex file.                                        
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                    MDG1TPORT INPUT SIGN COMMAND

----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES              |    DESCRIPTION                                                                  
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -inputhex          |    Input hex file name.                                                             
   -outputhex         |    Output Hash file name.                                                           
   -inputtxt          |    Input hex file name.                                                             
   -outputtext        |    Output Hash file name.                                                           
   -outputfiletype    |    Output hex file type.                                                            
   -igcks             |    Ignores line checksum while parsing the input hex file.                          
   -filetype          |    Input hex file type.                                                             
   -id                |    ID given to the hash for of each range.                                          
   -memoryType        |    Memory type.                                                                     
   -division          |    Specifies the division type.                                                     
   -pinpath           |    Pin file path.                                                                   
   -dummysignature    |    Dummy signature value.                                                           
   -signaturealgo     |    Signature algorithm name.                                                       
   -HSMfile           |    HSM file name.                                                                   
   -HSMconfig         |    HSM configuration type.                                                          
   -tctype            |    Trust center type Eg. BOSCH TRUST CENTER, VW TRUST CENTER                        
   -mode              |    Mode type eg. Online or Offline.                                             
   -oidpub            |    OID value.                                                                       
   -infoblockaddress  |    Infoblock start address.                                                     
   -infoblockcount    |    Infoblock count for which hash value to be calculated.                           
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                   MERGE COMMAND
                                                   
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION                                                                  
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-count            | Count of total number of file to be merged. By default it is 1.                 
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-file             | Hex file name.                                                                  
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-filetype         | Hex file type.                                                                  
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-overwrite        | Set overwrite either with true or false. By default it is false.                
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-mode             | Boolean attribute that specifies the Endianness. By default it is true.         
                  | True -> little endian                                                           
                  | False -> big endian Not mandatory                                               
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-igcks            | Boolean attribute to ignore line checksum. By default it is false               
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                    VDS BACK COMMAND

---------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES                   |    DESCRIPTION                                                             
---------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -type                   |    Type of the hex file                                                    
   -name                   |    Output file name.                                                       
   -infoblockaddress       |    start address of the infoblock.                                         
   -vdslog                 |    Logging for VDS.                                                        
   -fillvalue              |    Values to be filled in the gaps.                                        
   -vctrinfoblockaddress   |    Vector infoblock address.                                               
---------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                    VDS BACK COMMAND

---------------------------+------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES                   |    DESCRIPTION                                 
---------------------------+------------------------------------------------
   -type                   |    Type of the hex file                        
   -name                   |    Input file name.                            
   -infoblockaddress       |    start address of the infoblock.             
   -fillvalue              |    Values to be filled in the gaps.            
   -vctrinfoblockaddress   |    Vector infoblock address.                   
   -vdslog                 |    Logging for VDS.                            
   -vectortablelog         |    Logging for Vector table.                   
   -vectorinfolog          |    Logging for Vector infotable.               
   -count                  |    Total number of input file count.           
---------------------------+------------------------------------------------


                                               HEXCOMPARE COMMAND

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -file1      |    First input hex file for comparison.
   -file2      |    Second input hex file for comparison.
   -log        |    XML Comparison report path.
   -exit       |    Exits HexmodX if EXIT is "true" and if there are any difference found. It is "false" by default.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                    CHECKSUM COMMAND

-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES               |    DESCRIPTION
-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -startAddress       |    Start address of data range. Mandatory switch. 
   -endAddress         |    End address of data range. Mandatory Switch.  
   -startValue         |    Start Value for calculating checksum. Optional switch.
   -endValue           |    End Value for calculating checksum. Optional switch.
   -inverse            |    Inverse flag which is a boolean attribute. Optional switch.
   -alignement         |    Alignement flag which is a boolean attribute. Optional switch.
   -outputaddress      |    Output address where the calculated checksum is patched. Optional switch.
   -outputtxt          |    Text file to be generated which contains the calculated checksum for given range. 
                       |    Optional switch.
-----------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


                                                   DECOMPRESS COMMAND

------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -startaddress  |    Start address to be compressed. 
   -endaddress    |    End address to be compressed.   
   -at            |    Destination address where the compressed data will be placed.
   -outputfile    |    Output file name of the compressed hex file. 
   -type          |    Type of input HEX file.
   -fillpattern   |    Pattern to be filled in the gaps.
   -range         |    Specifies the number of data ranges to be compressed.
   -lyt           |    Layout of the output hex file.
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                                                   CERTINFO COMMAND
                                                   
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES              |    DESCRIPTION                                                                  
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -inputfile         |    Input hex file name.                                                                                                         
   -mode              |    Mode type eg. bigendian or littleendian.                                             
   -hsm_file          |    HSM configuration xml file name.                                                             
   -hsm_config        |    true or false to enable HSM configuration handling.  
   -infoblockaddress  |    Infoblock start address.     
   -output            |    Output xml file name.                                                       
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------